ous  and seeing it return to taliban control  led the musr to make a statement last  fall that went well beyond food  omar decided to step back from the  operations and put the women his wife's  sister and his two oldest daughters in  charge i said listen the only way to do  a change or to make a statement is you  have to  from inside to do something not through  words not through anything but through  action  what was the statement that you were  trying to make them women can do  anything oldest daughter talia is the  new manager of bistro arakasiya running  all the restaurants day-to-day  operations amman is manager in training  at the mclean location sometimes people  ask me for the manager and i'm like well  i am the manager  what does it mean to you to kind of be a  part of this statement that you're  making oh it makes me feel good that  they think that  i can manage a restaurant and run a  restaurant i want to be ceo of the  restaurants and just learn how to do  everything  the critically acclaimed restaurants the  women now in charge continue to expand  locations they attribute their success  to the customers and the recipes that  span generations from one mother to the  next i mean i learned this from my  mother so  that's how she made it that's how i made  it and  that's how i'm teaching  others to make it  and now passing again to the next what  is your dream for your  your daughters  as they grow up  to know who they are that's all i just  want them to to to know that they could  do anything they want to do they can run  a business they can be a ceo better  better what's your dream for their  futures for them to you know be  confident believe in themselves  um  be kind human beings  you know it's just also it's not just  about them it's about everyone and for  all those other girls needing to hear  you can do it jan crawford cbs mornings  mclean virginia  i love that when he was asked you know  what do you want your daughters to know  that they can do an